<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-asia</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:08:10Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-asia" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-12758?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-asia" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Three-way battle for power in world chess: Who will be elected FIDE president in Samarkand?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:48601a0841cb6a0ed9185cbeccf6bcf0351c2e8e14ea6f0e8014f4319fa9e430</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:07:27Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T18:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/three-way-battle-for-power-in-world-chess-who-will-be-elected-fide-president-in-samarkand/a-79413301--bc60333e85fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/three-way-battle-for-power-in-world-chess-who-will-be-elected-fide-president-in-samarkand/a-79413301?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The era of Russian presidents is coming to an end at the World Chess Federation (FIDE). Two Germans and one Kazakh are up for election. Among the issues at play are money, Kremlin influence, and unanswered questions.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Donald Trump hosts Xi Jinping for state dinner with tech titans. Follow live.</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5410b52261875c478ee2946e12b422fbe9f2f76448c8a4ffc33705dfc0832d51</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:08:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T13:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/donald-trump-hosts-xi-jinping-for-state-dinner-with-tech-titans-follow-live/live-79404511--d8b5960a2742.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/donald-trump-hosts-xi-jinping-for-state-dinner-with-tech-titans-follow-live/live-79404511?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump rolled out the red carpet for Chinese leader Xi Jinping, with the two having toasted each other at a lavish state dinner after their summit meeting. America's top tech bosses were also present at the dinner.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>EU finally clinching trade deals with Southeast Asian states</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f46e14f8730df4755bf0d29ca8702e075add5114d1ff618724eef57a76d1e977</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:07:27Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T11:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-finally-clinching-trade-deals-with-southeast-asian-states/a-79388278--8c0030248950.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-finally-clinching-trade-deals-with-southeast-asian-states/a-79388278?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After years of arduous negotiations, the EU is closing on a string of bilateral trade deals with countries in Southeast Asia. And yet, a bloc-to-bloc agreement between the EU and ASEAN remains a distant prospect.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Tensions between India and Bangladesh are in focus after Dhaka skipped the BRICS summit in Delhi</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:da7e27d206d8f729458d9e103d2fc095b5bd51ab2ab350e7cf37973b446fdca8</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:07:27Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T11:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/tensions-between-india-and-bangladesh-are-in-focus-after-dhaka-skipped-the-brics-summit-in-delhi/a-79410667--fb62a16b78a2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/tensions-between-india-and-bangladesh-are-in-focus-after-dhaka-skipped-the-brics-summit-in-delhi/a-79410667?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bangladesh's absence from the BRICS summit in New Delhi has raised fresh questions about strained ties. Ousted PM Sheikh Hasina's exile in India remains a major obstacle to normalizing relations.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Cockroach party demands Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar's resignation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:23a7c0ce3c0f6ac2bef433b0202e27cd1480f425d9bef0f535207d8fff3cf963</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:07:27Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T11:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-cockroach-party-demands-election-commissioner-gyanesh-kumar-s-resignation/live-79405879--428579042cfb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-cockroach-party-demands-election-commissioner-gyanesh-kumar-s-resignation/live-79405879?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">CJP's Abhijeet Dipke has alleged that the removal of more than 130 million names from draft electoral rolls is designed to benefit the BJP and weaken opposition parties. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>China's 13-year-old swimming star raises questions on child athletes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:70f077363db4607ebd815bd1a9efc0aa651755aa8b9335fb58051efa144d9cdb</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:07:27Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T14:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/china-s-13-year-old-swimming-star-raises-questions-on-child-athletes/a-79394183--95db71a677f9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/china-s-13-year-old-swimming-star-raises-questions-on-child-athletes/a-79394183?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Three gold medals and three Asian Games records have catapulted China's Yu Zidi, 13, into the sporting spotlight. She is far from the first teen prodigy, but should teens be competing at elite level?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Pakistan: Khan family arrests raise stakes ahead of protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fc8462ab4856a8487847b28c8c7ce80256762ba997c4825369fef2df46d1a977</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:07:27Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T13:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pakistan-khan-family-arrests-raise-stakes-ahead-of-protests/a-79392147--cb3db8a0de02.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pakistan-khan-family-arrests-raise-stakes-ahead-of-protests/a-79392147?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The sons of Pakistan's jailed former Prime Minister Imran Khan told DW their father is in ill health while being isolated from family and doctors. Other relatives have been detained ahead of a planned opposition protest.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India news: El Nino heat could kill 15,800 by February, report warns</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:18c2af5a01a5508ba9cb4564c8a9cad37b2b66cb809531288755de29e0c84c34</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:07:27Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T06:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-el-nino-heat-could-kill-15-800-by-february-report-warns/live-79382508--7338ab67b490.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-el-nino-heat-could-kill-15-800-by-february-report-warns/live-79382508?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A new Climate Impact Lab report warned that the El Nino heat will be most dangerous in places that are already hot and relatively poor. Meanwhile, Canada says PM Modi just confirmed a trip to the nation. Follow live.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Sri Lanka: 15 men jailed for life in 2019 Easter bombings</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e7793533beb3151e29bdeae67072deedab08861a0b0c8b81b75b218f8e64b6ca</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:07:27Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T05:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/sri-lanka-15-men-jailed-for-life-in-2019-easter-bombings/a-79382342--21e49f5e6a80.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/sri-lanka-15-men-jailed-for-life-in-2019-easter-bombings/a-79382342?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The 15 convicts have been given prison sentences of at least 200 years each, following a long trial in what was among Sri Lanka's deadliest attacks.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Nepal rejects 'sympathy,' asks for $20 mill after floods</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9f6982eb2bffaf4ac57472156c879fb8afee172993ba510214deca7333d1b183</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:07:27Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T12:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nepal-rejects-sympathy-asks-for-20-mill-after-floods/a-79372239--b0482f9bc73a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nepal-rejects-sympathy-asks-for-20-mill-after-floods/a-79372239?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">With Nepal still reeling from the devastating floods in August, Kathmandu is calling for climate justice and seeking compensation from the UN-backed Loss and Damage Fund, Environment Minister Geeta Chaudhary told DW.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Could we see MMA at the Olympics?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5d1b68e9624d96fc87bb1e1bab2e370c9709a450a134f1bbead5c5a298054bd4</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:07:27Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T12:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/could-we-see-mma-at-the-olympics/a-79369605--f76e8af14c92.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/could-we-see-mma-at-the-olympics/a-79369605?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Mixed martial arts has made its debut at the Asian Games this week. It takes the sport closer to the Olympics, but there are doubts about the next step — and the influence of the popular and lucrative UFC.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Male infertility is 'grossly underreported'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7c51e146751b26d206c50a6267770546903a7e5d2d6d5071afd12be82a716639</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:07:27Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T10:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/male-infertility-is-grossly-underreported/a-79368722--14a06576edd4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/male-infertility-is-grossly-underreported/a-79368722?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">It's not all on women anymore — doctors do test men for sperm count and motility. But still too few men get checked, possibly due to a misconception that a healthy sex life means healthy sperm. Spoiler: It doesn't.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>As Trump-Xi summit nears, Europe is caught in middle of US-China rivalry</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:45939eb17182fd7b234e2e15a738489b03ddebb70d30484a29a62e9627e6afe2</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:07:27Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T18:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/as-trump-xi-summit-nears-europe-is-caught-in-middle-of-us-china-rivalry/a-79356540--3c6355b77845.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/as-trump-xi-summit-nears-europe-is-caught-in-middle-of-us-china-rivalry/a-79356540?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">China's Xi Jinping is traveling to Washington this week. Regardless of what comes from his talks with US President Trump, the EU will likely remain stuck between erratic US trade policy and Beijing's export machine.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Nuclear power is back on Southeast Asia's energy agenda</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e435a2c9c8038121bc3354d5bc1691d09cd538a7e2ed7a695bad0711ff5fae63</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:08:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T13:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nuclear-power-is-back-on-southeast-asia-s-energy-agenda/a-79358744--70fdccf67ff5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nuclear-power-is-back-on-southeast-asia-s-energy-agenda/a-79358744?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Rising electricity demand, shocks in energy security and climate commitments are reviving long-stalled plans for nuclear power across Southeast Asia. But proponents of nuclear energy still face major obstacles.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India's road rage: When cars become weapons</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:36deefa7a61c3495455551df099144b52e3a3bcffb87f0b334bb75b72469ffc1</id><updated>2026-09-25T05:08:10Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T12:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-s-road-rage-when-cars-become-weapons/a-79355073--1e7f2ce4312e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-s-road-rage-when-cars-become-weapons/a-79355073?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Road disputes are turning violent across India, raising questions about status and impunity behind the wheel for drivers of expensive cars.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
